# {{jargon|or|jocular}} A person [[employ]]ed to work [[independently]] within a [[company]] in order to [[introduce]] [[innovation]] and to [[revitalize]] and [[diversify]] its [[business]].  Intrapreneurship is [[entrepreneurship]] practiced by people within established organizations.  An intrapreneur acts in ways typical of an [[entrepreneur]], while an employee of a preexisting institution, not as an owner, himself.